price they paid at the time that they would like to sell. In addition, an inactive market may impair Parent&#146;s ability to raise capital by selling shares or equity securities and may impair
its ability to acquire business partners by using the Parent Shares as consideration, which, in turn, could harm Parent&#146;s business. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B><I>The
trading price of the Parent Shares may be volatile, and holders of the Parent Shares could incur substantial losses. </I></B></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The stock
market in general has experienced extreme volatility in the wake of the <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">COVID-19</FONT> pandemic that has often been unrelated to the operating performance of particular companies. As a result of this volatility,
Lionheart&#146;s stockholders may not be able to sell their Parent Shares at or above the price paid for Lionheart securities. The market price for the Parent Shares may be influence by many factors, including: </P>
