expenses </B></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The Company enters into paid pilot and proof of concept (POC) agreements with the objective of achieving commercial agreements on the
activity. The other party to the agreement will reimburse the Company for expenditures on research and development. These reimbursements are offset in the profit or loss accounts against the related expenses (research and development expenses). Any
IP generated from this activity remains in the ownership of the Company. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The reimbursement from paid pilots and proof of concept projects for the six
months period ended June&nbsp;30, 2022, amounted to $1,020 ($555 for the six months period ended June&nbsp;30, 2021). </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>NOTE 3 - OTHER RECEIVABLES:
